CloudBurrow patch 61 to github.com/goccy/googlesqlite v0.3.1
(cloudburrow/cloudburrow#1516).

The bug: a collation on a STRING inside a STRUCT or an ARRAY
(`st STRUCT<a STRING COLLATE 'und:ci'>`, `arr ARRAY<STRING COLLATE
'und:ci'>`), and a table's DEFAULT COLLATE on such a STRING, failed
"GOOGLESQL_RET_CHECK failure (googlesql/analyzer/resolver_stmt.cc)
annotations != nullptr": the analyzer resolves a nested COLLATE only
with FEATURE_CREATE_TABLE_FIELD_ANNOTATIONS, and the catalog gave a
column only a top-level STRING's collation.

The fix, as BigQuery's collation reference documents ("A STRING field in
a STRUCT", "A STRING element in an ARRAY",
https://cloud.google.com/bigquery/docs/reference/standard-sql/collation-concepts):
- the analyzer has FEATURE_CREATE_TABLE_FIELD_ANNOTATIONS on;
- a CREATE TABLE records the collation of each STRING inside a STRUCT
  or an ARRAY column (its COLLATE, else the table's DEFAULT COLLATE
  unless its COLLATE is '') in ColumnSpec.FieldCollation, and the
  catalog gives the column an annotation map of the type's shape, so
  the analyzer propagates it to a field access, an UNNEST's element and
  a subscript (nested_collation.go);
- a comparison of an und:ci STRUCT or ARRAY (a STRUCT's =, !=, IN and
  CASE, IN UNNEST)
  compares its und:ci STRINGs case-folded, through a new function,
  googlesqlite_fold_collation.
Its test nested_collation_test.go fails without it.

